thority is the pinned internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md Sections 11.10 (11.10.1-11.10.5, AC-HOST-001 in the Appendix A acceptance table), 6.6, 11.1, 16.1, 15.1/15.3.\n2|\n3|Verify with your own instruments: (1) Whole-Story diff — story_final: the candidate tree against trunk e4e3e8834675cf3814effd3b2673b4931dfbf311 is the complete Story delta: four replayed checkpoints (2u34k1, 1tvg8e, 2ez769, z1yxg9 — originals efe119a, 5e54874, ae5a4cc, 244a7dc) plus this leaf; confirm every replayed commit is signed and its tree equals the original except LOGBOOK.md (resolutions kept every entry newest-first, trunk's 3lt2xv entry preserved); run the stale-copy audit yourself: for every path in `git diff --name-only 62d4463 e4e3e88` confirm the candidate does not revert trunk content (README -adopted docs, LOGBOOK 3lt2xv entry, internal/catalog/*); task-board.config.json equals trunk plus only the z1yxg9 rpcwire fuzz gate (state the exact diff); this leaf is test-only plus traceability/README/LOGBOOK — confirm no production file changed. (2) AC-HOST-001 — extract the acceptance row text yourself and map each clause to the suite: full mutual TLS, exact enrolled certificate/UUID/hello, no preauthentication effects, migration/downgrade refusals, fresh-key rotation, revocation of idle/live streams within one second, expiry, concurrent mutation-generation fencing, valid and invalid actual certificates, both role failures, stale/failed reads, recovery bypasses; the producer reports 14 of 15 rows driven and B8 (revocation ≤ 1 s) partial: next-dispatch fence and WatchGeneration measured < 1 s but idle-without-traffic self-close NOT satisfied — decide from the pinned text whether \"revocation of idle/live streams within one second\" is met by a caller-polled WatchGeneration design (z1yxg9's stated bound) or requires an in-package idle close: if the latter, grade P2 and say whether a minimal RED-first product change in internal/hostchannel belongs to this Story before story_final (the leaf may carry it) — do not accept a stated bound that contradicts a MUST. (3) Hostile matrix through the real channel — rerun the seven hostile rows and then plant your own vectors: unknown root, re-issued leaf under an enrolled root, spoofed hello ID with a valid cert, SAN naming another UUID, destination mismatch, disconnect at each phase boundary (assert no durable write via a state-dir census), replayed TLS flight and replayed hello (assert the class), oversize frames (state which cap fires), disclosure mismatch (contracts.rpc, Error version drift), silent peer past handshake/hello deadlines, mid-request stall against the RPC timeout, two concurrent connections from one peer, copied key authenticating until revoked, rotation admitting the new tuple only after enrollment with retire_at bounds, stale generation at dispatch and at a mutation boundary under concurrent mutation, Config-4 legacy route / RPC-4 hello / plaintext preface refusals, both role failures, unreadable trust store = integrity failure, retry with changed operation ID/body refused; each with the exact Section 15 class/exit. (4) OpenSSH loopback lane — rerun hostile_carrier_test.go: it must start an unprivileged sshd on 127.0.0.1 with a temp host key and a forced command, observe the exact ServeArgv server-side, prove TLS-first bytes, no PTY, bounded stderr; if it skips on this host the skip reason must be asserted and truthful; native Tailscale SSH must be recorded as not executed, never passed. (5) HC-* gates 10/10 with positive+negative vectors; the two z1yxg9 P3s closed (ax-host/2 same-family ALPN refused; bad-destination deadline hook). (6) Mutation — rerun mutations.py in an isolated copy (9 new + 26 prior probes; neutral passes; the documented client-cache SURVIVED), rerun each KILLED twice, plant at least four narrowing mutants of your own on the new assertion families (state-dir census ignoring one directory; disconnect classification collapsing transport_failure into authentication_failed; rotation admitting before enrollment for one peer; concurrent-mutation fence off by one generation) plus an applied harmless SURVIVED control; per-plant raw logs, subprocess exits, precise denominators. (7) Story-close items — ownership registry: AC-HOST-001 registered over the suite, new unevidenced bindings 11.10.1-11.10.4 + 16.1, 6.6/11.10 gaps refreshed, 11.10.5 unowned by design; reviewedOwnershipCanonicalSHA256 re-pinned over the merged registry (trunk rows + this Story's rows): recompute the projection digest independently, confirm every claimed clause line exists and each binding names an existing declaration driven by an acceptance case (plant a self-minted claim — refused), tracecheck counts reproduced; README/hostchannel README with test commands and no capability claim (no ax command); LOGBOOK newest-first with every Story entry plus trunk's 3lt2xv. (8) Hygiene — changed_paths carry no __pycache__/.pyc/stray plants or leftover sshd state; gofmt/vet clean; go test ./internal/hostchannel ./internal/rpcwire ./internal/hosttrust ./internal/traceability/... -count=1 and -race green; tracecheck and `cataloggen -adopted -output internal/catalog/catalog_gen.go -check` exit 0 on the exact tree.\n4|\n5|Method: isolated immutable probes only, never mutate the live Story worktree, index, branch or HEAD; never modify the preserved packet under .temp/TASK-260830-z1yxg9; no product edits, commits, checkpoints or integration; Curator go-testing-tools skill; all CI local; PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 for every harness; keep scratch small under .temp/TASK-260830-2x16gz/ and delete candidate copies when done. Attach TASK-260830-2x16gz_review-verdict-rev1.md and TASK-260830-2x16gz_review-evidence-rev1.tar.gz (a real gzip archive), complete the live merged checklist, then accept_cr(TASK-260830-2x16gz, revision=1, evidence=TASK-260830-2x16gz_review-verdict-rev1.md) or hand off changes requested with P1/P2/P3 classes named. Model: muse-spark xhigh (codex reviewers are out of quota until 2026-09-19). Canonical CLI /Users/iv/.curator/global/bin/task-board.","final_result":true}}}
