{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c3e5","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0afcb-4eda-7472-95f4-397cf45aa943"},"sequence":77,"recorded_at":1780531400000149,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"de9112ff-c6c5-4929-8606-bedba1c8b82d","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"de9112ff-c6c5-4929-8606-bedba1c8b82d","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"de9112ff-c6c5-4929-8606-bedba1c8b82d"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0afcb-8cde-78e1-9517-a3acf3ce8f2b"},"task_id":"01a0afcb-8cde-78e1-9517-a3acf3ce8f2b","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0afcb-8cde-78e1-9517-a3acf3ce8f2b","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260830-2x16gz/TASK-260830-2x16gz_producer.md`.\n1|Own TASK-260830-2x16gz (test-peer-auth-and-hostile-network-failures), the FINAL leaf of STORY-260830-1kiyj6 (peer-configuration-and-authentication). Predecessors on the Story branch, all accepted and checkpointed: 2u34k1 (host/peer identity), 1tvg8e (SSH transport and command boundary), 2ez769 (internal/hosttrust credentials, enrollment, rotation/revocation, authorization generations, Config-4 migration; ResolvedPaths pair), z1yxg9 (internal/rpcwire RPC 5.0.0 and internal/hostchannel Host Channel 1.0.0 with the HC-* fixture families; its verdict left two P3 notes you must close: an \"ax-host/2\" same-family ALPN refusal vector in TestVerifyPeerRefusals, and a shortened-deadline hook for the ~10 s TestInvalidActivation/bad_destination vector). You are the primary implementation-conformance owner for the pinned v0.6.0 Section 11.10.4 / AC-HOST-001 product gate (\"Drive the real Config-4 launch and RPC-5 dispatch on supported SSH/platform lanes: full mutual TLS, exact enrolled certificate/UUID/hello, no preauthentication effects, migration/downgrade refusals, fresh-key rotation, revocation of idle/live streams within one second, expiry and concurrent mutation-generation fencing; exercise valid and invalid actual certificates, both role failures, stale/failed reads and recovery bypasses; model fixtures alone never satisfy this gate\"), retaining the task's historical scope (unknown peers, key changes, spoofed host IDs, disconnects, replay, oversized frames, disclosure mismatches fail closed; Sections 6, 11.1, 16.1). Deliver an executable conformance suite over the landed production entries (hostchannel.Dial/Serve/Call, hosttrust enrollment/rotation/revocation/generation, config Config-4 selection, the SSH transport boundary of 1tvg8e) — no new product model: (1) real carrier lane — run the responder as a real child process behind a real OpenSSH loopback carrier where the host allows it (/usr/sbin/sshd is present: start an unprivileged sshd on 127.0.0.1 with a temp host key, a temp authorized_keys and a forced/exact command executing the AX responder over the ordered stdio stream; skip with an explicit, asserted reason if sshd cannot bind in this environment) and prove Section 11.10.1 end to end: TLS records are the first bytes on the stream, no PTY, no banner, stderr bounded; native Tailscale SSH is a stated bound (HC-PARITY by construction; record it as not executed, never as passed); (2) hostile-network matrix through the real channel — unknown peer (unenrolled root), key change (re-issued leaf under an enrolled root is not enrolled), spoofed host ID (valid cert for UUID A presenting hello ID B, and a cert whose SAN names B), destination mismatch, disconnect at every phase boundary (before TLS, mid-handshake, after handshake before hello, after hello, mid-request, mid-response — each yields transport_failure or the specified class with no partial effect and no durable write), replay (a recorded TLS flight and a recorded encrypted hello replayed on a fresh connection must be refused by TLS 1.3 itself — assert the failure class, and the nonce correlation rule for a replayed hello inside one session), oversized frames (8 MiB line, 5 MiB object, 1 MiB handshake cap versus Go's 256 KiB record cap — document which fires), disclosure mismatch (a peer presenting different identity facts in hello and certificate; contracts.rpc other than [\"5.0.0\"]; Structured Error version drift), timeout/race (silent peer past the handshake and hello deadlines; a peer stalling mid-request against the configured RPC timeout; two concurrent connections from one peer), custody (leaf private key read from a wrong-permission file or a foreign store refused by the ResolvedPaths pair; a copied key authenticates until revoked — assert both halves as the pinned text states), revocation and generation (revoke a live peer: idle and in-flight streams close within one second per the pinned text — measure it; rotation admits the new tuple only after explicit enrollment, retire_at bounds, no second rotation before revocation; a stale generation at dispatch and at a mutation boundary refused under concurrent mutation), migration/downgrade refusals (Config-4 selecting a legacy route, an RPC-4 hello on the host channel, a plaintext preface), both role failures (initiator refuses a bad server; responder refuses a bad client), stale/failed reads (an unreadable trust store or marker is an integrity failure, not \"absent\"), recovery bypasses (a retry that changes the operation ID or body is refused; no new-session/fresh-handle substitution); (3) every vector asserts the exact Section 15 class and exit and that nothing durable changed (census the state dir before/after); (4) the Section 11.10.5 upstream policy vectors are source evidence only — do not implement a policy reader and do not claim their synthetic passes as executed support; (5) narrowing mutants for every new assertion family with a shipped harness (per-plant raw logs, subprocess exits, an applied harmless SURVIVED control), plus the seven original conformance cases of this task re-derived with n-of-m through the authenticated channel; (6) a conformance matrix mapping every AC-HOST-001 clause, HC-* gate and hostile-network row to a test, a not-executed stated bound (native Tailscale SSH; platform lanes other than this host) or NOT APPLICABLE with owner. This is the FINAL leaf (story_final CR): carry the Story-close items — internal/traceability/ownership.v0.6.0.json bindings for 6.6/11.10/11.10.1-11.10.5/16.1 and the acceptance case AC-HOST-001 bound to the real conformance suite with honest coverage text (executed lanes versus stated bounds), reviewedOwnershipCanonicalSHA256 re-pinned (precedent Stories 3drr2m/3jqsx1/3m2mw8/2jylym); README sections for internal/hostchannel/rpcwire (if missing) and your suite with test commands and no capability claim (no ax command exists); LOGBOOK entry; the candidate's task-board.config.json must remain byte-identical to trunk except the rpcwire fuzz gate already added by z1yxg9 (if you add a conformance command, say so explicitly and keep it bounded). Managed Story worktree contract: .temp/STORY-260830-1kiyj6/worktree on branch task-board/story/STORY-260830-1kiyj6 whose tip is the z1yxg9 checkpoint; the preserved packet directories under .temp are read-only; leave the candidate UNCOMMITTED, never commit on the Story branch, never edit .task-board directly, never self-accept; origin/main has moved to e4e3e88 (release-agnostic validation command 21) — run task-board worktree refresh-candidate TASK-260830-2x16gz first and restore any trunk-changed path the refresh left stale with a single-path git checkout HEAD -- <path>; before handoff verify git status shows only candidate paths (no __pycache__, no .pyc; PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1). Evidence contract as in the repository DoD. Read the Curator-managed go-testing-tools skill first; all CI local; run the full configured validation suite once before the handoff; hand off no later than 3.5 hours in (an 8-point leaf: if the full matrix cannot be finished, hand off a reviewable slice with the remaining rows enumerated precisely — the Story-close items are mandatory). Attach TASK-260830-2x16gz_results.md, TASK-260830-2x16gz_conformance-matrix.md and TASK-260830-2x16gz_producer-evidence.tar.gz (a real gzip archive), keep the checklist current, then task-board handoff TASK-260830-2x16gz --role developer and exit promptly. Canonical CLI /Users/iv/.curator/global/bin/task-board. Model: muse-spark max. The independent reviewer will be muse-spark xhigh while codex is out of quota.","final_result":true}}}
