are not candidate paths; for candidate paths such as LOGBOOK.md, README.md, internal/traceability/ownership.v0.6.0.json, traceability.go, traceability_test.go, tracecheck main_test.go merge by hand so that trunk's lines are all present and your additions remain — the diff against HEAD must be purely additive for LOGBOOK/README apart from figure lines you rewrite, and the ownership registry must contain trunk's rows plus yours); task-board.config.json must equal HEAD (or HEAD plus only what your Story's earlier checkpoints intentionally carry — state which); recompute and re-pin reviewedOwnershipCanonicalSHA256 over the merged registry, refresh the tracecheck/report pins and README figures; (4) rerun the full 26-command suite from the worktree's task-board.config.json plus your own suites; (5) verify `git status` shows exactly your candidate paths (no __pycache__/.pyc), attach UPDATED outcomes TASK-260830-2x16gz_results-rev2.md (the refresh/reconcile record with exact commands, OIDs, every resolution's checkpoint binding, the stale-copy audit table path-by-path, the digest re-pin), TASK-260830-2x16gz_conformance-matrix-rev2.md and TASK-260830-2x16gz_producer-evidence-rev2.tar.gz (a real gzip archive) — a handoff without a new or updated task-scoped outcome is cancelled as handoff_unsatisfied; (6) task-board handoff TASK-260830-2x16gz --role developer and exit promptly. Do not re-implement or change product code beyond the reconciliation; never commit on the Story branch; never edit .task-board directly; never self-accept; never edit the control root. Canonical CLI /Users/iv/.curator/global/bin/task-board. Model: muse-spark max.","final_result":true}}}
