{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c5ef","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0afcb-4eda-7472-95f4-397cf45aa943"},"sequence":338,"recorded_at":1780531400000671,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"de9112ff-c6c5-4929-8606-bedba1c8b82d","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"de9112ff-c6c5-4929-8606-bedba1c8b82d","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"de9112ff-c6c5-4929-8606-bedba1c8b82d"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0afcc-60c0-76f3-90f6-733ffc59b814"},"task_id":"01a0afcc-60c0-76f3-90f6-733ffc59b814","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0afcc-60c0-76f3-90f6-733ffc59b814","chunk":"Read text file `README.md`.\n(3039 line(s) above)\n3040|```bash\n3041|go run ./internal/catalog/cmd/cataloggen -metadata internal/catalog/catalog.v0.6.0.json -contracts internal/specpin/v0.6.0.lock.json -output internal/catalog/catalog_gen.go -check\n3042|```\n3043|\n3044|## Specification-to-Code Ownership Gate\n3045|\n3046|[`internal/traceability`](internal/traceability) provides the read-only\n3047|repository gate used by CI. Its reviewed\n3048|[`ownership.v0.6.0.json`](internal/traceability/ownership.v0.6.0.json)\n3049|registry independently enumerates implementation owners for all 63 current\n3050|contract rows, 36 pinned or catalog-referenced normative section keys, 132\n3051|executable acceptance cases, 65 exact section bindings with their declared\n3052|coverage, 7 disclosed unowned sections, and 32 exact fixture identities or\n3053|Appendix D anchors. The v0.4.3 projection is checked as an owned 55-contract subset,\n3054|and the superseded v0.5.0 registry is checked as an owned legacy projection.\n3055|The generated v0.6.0 catalog also carries the reviewed schema/version/self-field\n3056|contracts used by canonical object identity calculation; generator validation\n3057|binds each row to a pinned contract and rejects duplicate, unsupported,\n3058|malformed, or digest-drifted metadata.\n3059|\n3060|The production validator re-verifies the exact source lock and reviewed catalog\n3061|metadata, refuses stale generated output, requires every production and test\n3062|owner to resolve to a real Go declaration, and rejects gaps, duplicates,\n3063|self-minted keys, partial or malformed reads, and semantic ownership drift.\n3064|GitHub Actions invokes the gate directly before generation, tests, vet, and\n3065|build:\n3066|\n3067|```bash\n3068|go run ./internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck\n3069|go run ./internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck -section 6.2\n3070|```\n3071|\n3072|The repeated `-section` form is the Story-scope production gate. It resolves\n3073|each assigned subsection, and every heading in a same-top-level range, against\n3074|the immutable v0.5.0 inventory. Every exact `section_binding` must name its own\n3075|production declaration and executable acceptance case, and must additionally\n3076|discharge the whole section it claims. A generic top-level source pin is not a\n3077|scoped implementation owner. Malformed, nonexistent, unpinned, or otherwise\n3078|unowned assignments fail closed.\n3079|\n3080|### Declared coverage and what the gate can decide\n3081|\n3082|A binding that names a real Go declaration and a real acceptance case used to be\n3083|enough. It is not: `section:2.2` named `validateSessionRecordCommon`, which\n3084|validates one enum and a name grammar, while Section 2.2 is the twenty-two\n3085|unconditional lease and replica invariants; `section:18.4` named\n3086|`OpenProjection` while Section 18.4 is audit retention and no retention code\n3087|exists. A Story assigned either section would have found it already owned and\n3088|could have done nothing.\n3089|\n3090|Every `section_binding` now declares a `coverage` level, and the gate recomputes\n3091|that level rather than believing it. The denominator is measured from\n3092|[`internal/specdoc`](internal/specdoc): the RFC 2119 clause lines the pinned\n3093|`SPEC.md` carries under the section's own heading and its subheadings. The\n3094|numerator is the `clauses` the binding enumerates, each of which must name a\n3095|clause of that inventory, quote it verbatim beginning on the exact `SPEC.md`\n3096|line it occupies, and be discharged by an acceptance case the binding itself\n3097|owns.\n3098|\n3099|| Level | Meaning | Admitted as an assigned scope |\n3100|| --- | --- | --- |\n3101|| `full` | every normative clause of the section is enumerated and discharged | yes |\n3102|| `partial` | at least half are | no |\n3103|| `sliver` | fewer than half are | no |\n3104|| `unevidenced` | none are; the registry makes no clause-level claim | no |\n3105|| `unmeasured` | the obligation scanner finds no clause line under the section at all | no |\n3106|\n3107|`unmeasured` is the honest name for what used to be called `declarative` and\n3108|used to be admitted. The scanner matches uppercase RFC 2119 keywords, so a\n3109|section that states its obligations as a table scores zero and was read as\n3110|carrying no obligation. That is false, and the first revision of this gate\n3111|reproduced the very bug it was built to remove: `-section 15.2`, the eighteen-row\n3112|normative exit-code registry, exited 0 with nothing in the tree implementing it,\n3113|and so did `-section 7.3`, the closed Provider Manifest. Nineteen of the 157\n3114|pinned headings are in that class - 7.3, 10.8.1, 13.5, 13.12, 13.14.1-13.14.5,\n3115|14.3, 14.6, 15.2, 16.6, 16.7, 18.2, 19.4 and Appendices A, B and C - and\n3116|`TestUnmeasuredCoverageIsAScannerBlindSpotNotAnAbsenceOfObligation` measures\n3117|that every one of them has a substantive body, so not one is a heading with\n3118|nothing to discharge. Keyword absence is now a failure to measure, never a\n3119|coverage claim.\n3120|\n3121|A binding below `full` must also name its gap, `unmeasured` included, and the\n3122|gap has to name the section as a whole identifier - so a sentence about 6.55 is\n3123|not a gap about 6.5 - and name the production declaration the binding is\n3124|registered to. `unowned_sections` records a section this repository does not\n3125|implement at all, with a gap and the evidence for it; an unowned entry may not\n3126|cover a section the generated catalog requires an owner for, so it is a\n3127|disclosure and never an exemption. Every one of these fields is inside the\n3128|reviewed projection digest, so none of them can be self-minted.\n3129|\n3130|This is what the gate decides, and it is less than semantic coverage. It decides\n3131|that a claimed clause is a real obligation of the claimed section, that it is\n3132|quoted verbatim at the line it occupies, that the discharging acceptance case is\n3133|registered and owned by the binding, and that the declared level equals the\n3134|measured ratio. **It cannot decide that the named acceptance case exercises the\n3135|clause's meaning.** A binding could enumerate every clause of a section and\n3136|point all of them at one weak test, and the gate would admit it. That residual\n3137|class - a complete enumeration discharged by inadequate tests - is not covered\n3138|here and is not claimed to be.\n3139|\n3140|It also cannot see an obligation stated without an RFC 2119 keyword, which is\n3141|why `unmeasured` is refused rather than admitted: the gate reports that it could\n3142|not measure the section instead of inferring that there was nothing to measure.\n3143|And the gap-quality check is a tightening rather than a proof - a sentence that\n3144|names both its section and its production declaration and still says nothing\n3145|useful is admitted, and the gate cannot decide otherwise.\n3146|\n3147|### Measured coverage of this repository\n3148|\n3149|`tracecheck` prints the ratio it measured rather than a sentence about it:\n3150|\n3151|```text\n3152|section coverage: bindings=60 full=2 partial=6 sliver=4 unevidenced=44 unmeasured=4 unowned=11 clauses_discharged=49/511\n3153|```\n3154|\n3155|Sixty section bindings discharge 49 of the 511 normative clauses their\n3156|sections carry. Two bindings are `full` (Section 6.2, whose single clause is the\n3157|native-Windows `conpty` requirement, discharged by the positive\n3158|`TestEveryPinnedReaderHasPositiveNativeWindowsAndWSL2Lanes` lanes together\n3159|with the negative `TestDecodeRefusesNonConptyBackendOnNativeWindows` legacy\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
