{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000cbfd","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0afcb-4eda-7472-95f4-397cf45aa943"},"sequence":1113,"recorded_at":1780531400002221,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"de9112ff-c6c5-4929-8606-bedba1c8b82d","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"de9112ff-c6c5-4929-8606-bedba1c8b82d","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"de9112ff-c6c5-4929-8606-bedba1c8b82d"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0afd9-4fba-7091-ac84-67a68c0b985a"},"task_id":"01a0afd9-4fba-7091-ac84-67a68c0b985a","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0afd9-4fba-7091-ac84-67a68c0b985a","chunk":"Read text file `/tmp/rev4-logs/results-rev3.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-2x16gz results rev3 — base refresh + reconcile + full revalidation\n2|\n3|Role: developer (republish run, no re-implementation).\n4|Rev1 outcomes (`TASK-260830-2x16gz_results.md`, `..._conformance-matrix.md`,\n5|`..._producer-evidence.tar.gz`) remain the implementation evidence; rev2\n6|(`..._results-rev2.md`, `..._conformance-matrix-rev2.md`) remains the first\n7|refresh record. This rev3 record covers the second base refresh (onto\n8|`fc67abd` after CR1 went stale via `integration_base_moved`), the candidate\n9|reconcile, and the rerun of the full configured suite plus the shipped\n10|mutation battery on the new base. All implementation ratios and stated bounds\n11|from rev1 stand unchanged; registry/report figures moved additively with\n12|trunk (see §2–§4).\n13|\n14|## 1. Refresh record\n15|\n16|Story branch `task-board/story/STORY-260830-1kiyj6`, worktree\n17|`.temp/STORY-260830-1kiyj6/worktree`.\n18|\n19|- Pre-refresh tip: `c3de159762f3e3d0a926ece0b0d4231abb669562` (z1yxg9 replay).\n20|- Old trunk base: `e4e3e8834675cf3814effd3b2673b4931dfbf311`.\n21|- Fresh authority: `origin/main = fc67abdfc3888d6683b1eb89bc248e089ca6aca3`\n22|  (STORY-260830-315721, STORY-260830-2rqigd, STORY-260830-1oqfec, the PR48\n23|  routing change, plus board-state records).\n24|- Commands: `task-board worktree refresh-candidate TASK-260830-2x16gz`\n25|  (+ `--replay-resolutions /tmp/rev3/resolutions-rev3.json`, two resolutions,\n26|  accumulated across the two stops).\n27|- Outcome: `refresh_advanced`, new tip\n28|  `9636508e5a1d1fd3bd2fbd21e4cadcddd88aeecd`.\n29|\n30|Replayed checkpoints (original -> replayed, all `git verify-commit` Good,\n31|parent chain reaches `fc67abd`):\n32|\n33|| # | Original | Replayed | Subject |\n34||---|---|---|---|\n35|| 1 | `14d1176` | `3337a0b04c474f4bd1d300b8c4e0aa32cbfe0e99` | 2u34k1 host/peer identity |\n36|| 2 | `4677a87` | `6ebe7748c81377939fec88cc0509337957389488` | 1tvg8e SSH transport |\n37|| 3 | `a14f718` | `c3fec77d3a73be5bdecbb090178cf1103893d03c` | 2ez769 credentials/config4 |\n38|| 4 | `c3de159` | `9636508e5a1d1fd3bd2fbd21e4cadcddd88aeecd` | z1yxg9 RPC envelope/hello |\n39|\n40|Checkpoints 1–2 replayed without conflict. Unlike rev2, this cycle stopped\n41|twice on non-LOGBOOK content conflicts (template\n42|`{\"version\":1,\"branch_oid\",\"trunk_oid\",\"candidate_tree_oid\",\"resolutions\":[...]}`,\n43|header copied from each retained\n44|`.temp/base-refresh/replay-*/resolution-template.json`, both headers\n45|identical):\n46|\n47|| Resolution | `checkpoint_oid` (REBASE_HEAD) | Path | Replacement sha256 | Bytes |\n48||---|---|---|---|---|\n49|| 1 | `a14f718288902627340f5f8086e9c984e060191a` | `internal/secprim/census_test.go` | `7a99d2da0aad39657c98d42f109c7672a01b1b84ce1f7988c6129781dc1bace5` | 28287 |\n50|| 2 | `c3de159762f3e3d0a926ece0b0d4231abb669562` | `internal/traceability/traceability.go` | `4497782a1f1814a7befbed6eca6bcbe15e589d1f8904a94376fd2692c0584a8f` | 48524 |\n51|\n52|Resolution 1 rule: same-anchor row insertion — trunk's 1 `provhost`\n53|census row plus the checkpoint's 6 credential/custody rows are all kept\n54|(trunk row first, then the 6 checkpoint rows as new rows). The census\n55|checks are order-independent set checks (no row-count assertion), so the\n56|union is exact; the merged file is `gofmt`-clean and parses.\n57|\n58|Resolution 2 rule: the pinned `reviewedOwnershipCanonicalSHA256` line\n59|conflicted (trunk `39087ef8…` vs checkpoint `5102d3bc…`) while the\n60|registry itself auto-merged (trunk's 65 bindings + the checkpoint's 7\n61|gap-line enrichments). Neither pin fits the merged registry, so the\n62|replacement re-pins to the recomputed canonical digest `eefba9e5…` of\n63|the merged bytes. The recompute method (standalone Go over verbatim\n64|projection structs, no custom marshalers in the path) was verified by\n65|reproducing BOTH known digests first: trunk registry -> `39087ef8…`,\n66|`c3de159` registry -> `5102d3bc…`.\n67|\n68|Replay-fidelity verification (all four checkpoints):\n69|\n70|- `git verify-commit` Good on all four replayed commits.\n71|- Per-commit patch paths identical: `git diff <o>^ <o> --name-only` equals\n72|  `git diff <n>^ <n> --name-only` for all four pairs (4/4 identical).\n73|- Resolution blobs byte-identical in the replayed commits (`git show\n74|  c3fec77:internal/secprim/census_test.go` sha256 = `7a99d2da…`;\n75|  `git show 9636508:internal/traceability/traceability.go` sha256 =\n76|  `4497782a…`).\n77|- LOGBOOK.md auto-merged at every step with zero line losses in both\n78|  directions (`comm` of sorted lines vs trunk and vs `c3de159`: both\n79|  empty); no LOGBOOK resolution was needed this cycle. Note on the\n80|  brief's literal check: `git diff <original> <replayed> --stat` compares\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
