{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000cc27","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0afcb-4eda-7472-95f4-397cf45aa943"},"sequence":1134,"recorded_at":1780531400002263,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"de9112ff-c6c5-4929-8606-bedba1c8b82d","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"de9112ff-c6c5-4929-8606-bedba1c8b82d","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"de9112ff-c6c5-4929-8606-bedba1c8b82d"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0afd9-63dd-76a0-9a89-5cab3bc8a06e"},"task_id":"01a0afd9-63dd-76a0-9a89-5cab3bc8a06e","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0afd9-63dd-76a0-9a89-5cab3bc8a06e","chunk":"Read text file `/tmp/rev4-logs/results-rev3.md`.\n(79 line(s) above)\n80|  brief's literal check: `git diff <original> <replayed> --stat` compares\n81|  full trees and therefore always shows the 321-file trunk delta after a\n82|  base move; the per-commit patch equivalence above is the operative\n83|  fidelity check, and it holds exactly.\n84|\n85|## 2. Stale-copy audit (carried candidate vs new HEAD)\n86|\n87|Pre-refresh safety: the 11 tracked candidate files, their leaf diffs vs\n88|`c3de159`, and both new test files were copied to `/tmp/rev3/` (kept in\n89|the evidence tar) before reconciling.\n90|\n91|After `refresh_advanced` the worktree held 152 entries: the 13 candidate\n92|paths plus 139 stale carried copies. Every stale path is in the trunk\n93|delta `e4e3e88..fc67abd` (321 files; machine-checked, zero unexplained),\n94|so all 139 were restored with `git checkout HEAD -- <paths>`:\n95|\n96|| Stale group | Paths | Disposition |\n97||---|---|---|\n98|| `internal/provhost` (18), `fencing` (16), `sessprofile` (15), `resumesmoke` (14), `matjournal` (12), `crashgate` (11), `sessrepo` (10), `sessckpt` (9), `sessstate` (4), `sessquery` (1), `secprim/census_test.go` (1), `environ/census_test.go` (1) | 112 | trunk-landed story files reverted/deleted by the carry; restored to `HEAD` |\n99|| `.task-board/.activity` (13) + `.task-board/.../progress.md` (13) | 26 | board-checkout artifacts inside the worktree; restored to `HEAD` |\n100|| `task-board.config.json` | 1 | restored to `HEAD`; verified byte-identical (`git diff HEAD` empty). `HEAD` = trunk `-adopted` command + the story's rpcwire fuzz gate (both intentional, as in rev2); this leaf adds nothing |\n101|\n102|Six candidate paths are also in the trunk delta and were hand-merged\n103|(base `c3de159` blob, ours = stale leaf copy, theirs = new `HEAD`):\n104|\n105|| Candidate path | Merge |\n106||---|---|\n107|| `internal/traceability/ownership.v0.6.0.json` | 3-way semantic union, machine-verified: key sets = exact union (70 ownership / 132 acceptance / 7 unowned); leaf adds 5 section bindings + `AC-HOST-001` + 2 gap mods + `11.10.5` unowned text; trunk adds 30 cases + 4 bindings + 7 gap mods + `2.2` unowned removal; modified-key sets disjoint. Single textual conflict (acceptance-array same-anchor insert) spliced trunk-first (30 trunk entries, then `AC-HOST-001`), JSON-validated |\n108|| `internal/traceability/traceability.go` | both sides changed only the pin line; final = `HEAD` + recomputed pin `d3eca906…` over the merged registry (same verified method as resolution 2) |\n109|| `internal/traceability/traceability_test.go`, `internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck/main_test.go` | figure conflicts resolved to trunk + leaf-delta pins (132 cases / 65 bindings / full 2 / partial 6 / sliver 4 / unevidenced 49 / unmeasured 4 / unowned 7 / clauses 49/535); trunk's `2.2`/`2.4`/`18.4` expectation updates kept via auto-merge |\n110|| `README.md` | single figure conflict resolved to 132/65/7; leaf hostile-suite paragraph + 2 tool-table rows auto-merged in place with correct context |\n111|| `LOGBOOK.md` | leaf entry block (9 lines) inserted verbatim after the first `## 2026-09-17` heading; `git diff HEAD` = 9 insertions, 0 deletions |\n112|\n113|Seven candidate paths are clean carries (not in the trunk delta):\n114|5 tracked `internal/hostchannel` files (base blobs identical across the\n115|refresh, diffs untouched) plus the 2 new `hostile_*_test.go` files.\n116|\n117|Digest re-pin: `reviewedOwnershipCanonicalSHA256` is now\n118|`d3eca9063c0f7b7a6abc38a7f53c5d6c01bdbc076886e19a2c66e0a87693e58a`\n119|(canonical sha256 of the merged registry; `tracecheck` exits 0 and\n120|`TestVerifyRepositoryAcceptsExactOwnership` passes on it).\n121|\n122|Final `git status`: exactly the 13 candidate paths (11 modified + 2 new),\n123|no `__pycache__`, no `.pyc` (`PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1` throughout),\n124|no staged changes. Candidate left UNCOMMITTED on the story branch; no\n125|commit, no push, no board edit from this run beyond status/evidence.\n126|\n127|## 3. Full validation rerun on `9636508` (all observed this run)\n128|\n129|Configured suite = 27 commands from `task-board.config.json`\n130|(`spawn.worktree_isolation.validation.commands`):\n131|\n132|| # | Command | Result |\n133||---|---|---|\n134|| 1 | `gofmt` clean check | pass |\n135|| 2 | `go build ./...` | pass |\n136|| 3 | `go vet ./...` | pass |\n137|| 4 | `go test ./... -count=1 -v` | exit 0, 37 packages ok, 0 FAIL, 21523 `--- PASS` (indented `--- FAIL` lines in the log are mutant-harness log echoes, e.g. resumesmoke `TestSmokeMutantsAreKilled` quoting killed-mutant subprocess output; zero top-level `^--- FAIL`, zero `^FAIL`) |\n138|| 5 | `go test ./... -race -count=1` | exit 0, 37 ok, 0 FAIL, 0 data races |\n139|| 6 | `go test ./... -cover -count=1` | exit 0 (hostchannel 84.1, hosttrust 76.3, rpcwire 97.8, traceability 86.2, tracecheck 88.5) |\n140|| 7–20 | 14 fuzz smokes (rpcwire 1, scalar 1, canonicaljson 4, secconftest 8) | 14/14 pass |\n141|| 21 | `tracecheck` | exit 0; `acceptance_cases=132 ... bindings=65 ... unowned=7 clauses_discharged=49/535` |\n142|| 22 | `cataloggen -adopted ... -check` | exit 0, no generated drift |\n143|| 23–24 | `GOOS=linux/windows go build ./...` | exit 0 both |\n144|| 25 | JSON parse over tracked `*.json` | pass |\n145|| 26 | `task-board validate` | exit 0; 191 pre-existing board-hygiene issues, 0 referencing this task/story |\n146|| 27 | `git diff --check` | clean |\n147|\n148|Own suites (this run):\n149|\n150|- `go test ./internal/hostchannel -run 'TestHostile' -count=1 -v`: exit 0,\n151|  54 `--- PASS`, 0 FAIL. `TestHostileRealCarrierOpenSSH` PASS (0.30 s —\n152|  OpenSSH loopback lane executed, not skipped). The single SKIP is\n153|  `TestHostileSSHHelperResponder`, the helper-process guard (skips unless\n154|  invoked as the forced-command child — by design).\n155|- `python3 internal/hostchannel/mutations.py --output\n156|  .temp/TASK-260830-2x16gz/mutations-hostchannel-rev3`: exit 0, 33/33\n157|  registered probes executed, full behavioral suite per plant, sources\n158|  untouched (overlay). Verdicts: 31 killed, 1 neutral passed, 1\n159|  survived (`client-cache`, exit 0, the documented harmless control —\n160|  caching client sessions while the server issues no tickets changes\n161|  no behavior). All 9 new narrowing probes killed by their named\n162|  vectors: `alpn-same-family` by\n163|  `TestVerifyPeerRefusals/alpn-same-family`, `oversize-dispatch` by\n164|  `TestHostileOversizedFrames/dispatch_line_8mib_plus_one`,\n165|  `stale-client-rebind` by\n166|  `TestHostileRecoveryBypass/stale_binding_never_rebinds`,\n167|  `rpc-contracts` by\n168|  `TestHostileDisclosureMismatch/responder_contracts_drift`,\n169|  `error-version-drift` by\n170|  `TestHostileDisclosureMismatch/error_version_drift`,\n171|  `truncated-dispatch-ignored` by\n172|  `TestHostileDisconnectPhases/mid_request_close`, `snapshot-integrity`\n173|  by `TestHostileStaleReadsAreIntegrityFailures/corrupt_store`,\n174|  `correlation-health` by\n175|  `TestHostileRecoveryBypass/response_id_mismatch_refused`,\n176|  `nonce-static` by `TestHostileReplayNonceFreshness`. Prior 24 probes:\n177|  22 killed, neutral passed, `client-cache` survived as designed.\n178|  (Denominator note: rev1 text says \"26 prior\"; the shipped registry —\n179|  byte-identical then and now — holds 24 prior + 9 new = 33, and this\n180|  rerun executed all 33. Observed counts above are exact.)\n181|\n182|## 4. Coverage restatement (unchanged from rev1/rev2)\n183|\n184|- Hostile rows: 7 of 7 driven (`Dial`/`Serve`/`Call`).\n185|- AC-HOST-001 rows: 14 of 15 fully driven; B8 partial (measured bound).\n186|- HC-* families: 10 of 10. P3 notes: 2 of 2 closed.\n187|- Stated bounds unchanged (native Tailscale SSH, non-host lanes, idle\n188|  self-close measured, 11.10.5 policy reader by design, no `ax` CLI).\n189|- Registry/report figures moved with trunk: 102->132 cases, 61->65\n190|  bindings, 8->7 unowned, 17/487->49/535 clauses (trunk +30 cases /\n191|  +4 bindings / -1 unowned / +32 discharged clauses composed with the\n192|  leaf's +1 case / +5 bindings / -4 unowned; verified by the passing\n193|  report test, not by arithmetic alone).\n194|- No unsupported capability advertised; README/hostchannel docs and the\n195|  traceability bindings already updated in the carried candidate.\n196|\n197|## 5. Handoff evidence (rev3)\n198|\n199|- `TASK-260830-2x16gz_results-rev3.md` (this file)\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
